# The ledger of `ui`: what a program with windows of the system's own
# widgets can do, one block per capability, and what Rebel answers. The
# lists are this machine's, 2026-11-22. Go's standard library holds no user
# interface, so its column is `github.com/andlabs/ui`
# v0.0.0-20200610043537-70a69d6ae31e (libui: each system's own widgets, the
# manner this package takes), read by `go doc -all`. Python's is `tkinter`, its
# standard library's, with `tkinter.ttk`, `messagebox`, `filedialog`,
# `simpledialog`, `colorchooser`, `font`, `dnd` and `scrolledtext`, its
# public classes and functions listed from the modules' declarations by
# `ast`, since this Python 3.15.2 is built without `_tkinter` and `dir()`
# cannot import it; a method is named after its class. Rust's standard
# library holds no user interface and no crate of each system's own widgets
# is Rust's common one, so its column is `-` but where Tauri 2.12.5, which
# this machine holds and whose public structs were looked up in it, names
# the same thing: the web view and the tray.

capability ui/app  a user interface opened on the system's own widgets or with no screen, and closed
  heroes  ui.open, ui.close, ui.is_native, ui.App, ui.Backend
  go      ui.Main, ui.Quit, ui.OnShouldQuit
  rust    -
  python  tkinter.Tk, tkinter.NoDefaultRoot
  note    an app is a handle the program closes, told when `main` returns where it did not (spec § 13); `ui.Main` runs the program inside the system's loop and `tkinter.mainloop` never returns, where here the program asks for each event

capability ui/events  what the person did, asked for and waited on for a bounded time
  heroes  ui.wait, ui.Event
  go      Button.OnClicked, Checkbox.OnToggled, Combobox.OnSelected, Entry.OnChanged, MultilineEntry.OnChanged, RadioButtons.OnSelected, Slider.OnChanged, Window.OnClosing
  rust    -
  python  tkinter.mainloop, tkinter.Event, tkinter.EventType, tkinter.Misc.bind
  note    the three libraries call the program back from the system's loop; the language has no closures, so `wait` answers a variant naming the widget by the handle the program holds, and the program matches it (README § B3)

capability ui/inject  what a person does, given by the program, to drive a test or a headless demo
  heroes  ui.inject, ui.Input
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  tkinter.Misc.event_generate
  note    on the native side each input goes through the system's own path (`performClick` on macOS), so its event comes as the person's would

capability ui/keys-pressed  a key pressed by the program as the person's keyboard presses it, through the system's own path
  heroes  ui.press_key
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    wxWidgets' `wxUIActionSimulator`; native on macOS (the key goes down and up through `NSApp.sendEvent`, the window made the key window of the active application first), Windows pending, Linux pending; on the headless side a key chooses the menu item whose shortcut it is

capability ui/edit-menu  the system's Edit menu in every text widget: undo, redo, cut, copy, paste, delete and select all, by the mouse and by their keys
  heroes  ui.text_field, ui.text_area
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    wxWidgets' standard identifiers `wxID_UNDO` to `wxID_SELECTALL`; on macOS the arm's menu bar holds the standard Edit menu after the window's first menu, each item sending AppKit's own action to the widget with the keys (without it Command+C and the rest reached no text widget); Windows' and GTK's edit controls take Ctrl+C and the rest themselves (their arms pending)

capability ui/headless  the widgets kept and laid out with no screen, and drawn as text
  heroes  ui.render, ui.Backend
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    every machine draws the same lines, so a demo's transcript is a test

capability ui/native-windows  the native side on Windows, by Win32
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -

capability ui/native-linux  the native side on Linux, by GTK
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -

capability ui/webview  the system's web view as a widget, with a bridge to its scripts
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    tauri::WebviewWindow, tauri::Webview
  python  -
  note    the kind `ui.Kind.webview` and the event `ui.Event.message` stand in the face for it

capability ui/mailbox  a thread's message to the user interface, through feature 2647's mailbox
  heroes  pending
  go      ui.QueueMain
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    until it lands, a thread's work is read by the program when a `timer` fires

capability ui/window  a window: its title, its size, whether the person may resize it, and its close button asked
  heroes  ui.window, ui.set_text, ui.set_size, ui.set_resizable, ui.rect_of, ui.Event.close_asked
  go      ui.NewWindow, Window.SetTitle, Window.Title, Window.SetChild, Window.OnClosing
  rust    -
  python  tkinter.Toplevel, tkinter.Wm
  note    a window lays its children out in a column, so it needs no child of its own, `Window.SetChild`'s

capability ui/boxes  widgets side by side and one under another, with spacing, padding, and the room left shared by weights
  heroes  ui.row, ui.column, ui.set_spacing, ui.set_fit, ui.default_fit, ui.Fit, ui.Align
  go      ui.NewHorizontalBox, ui.NewVerticalBox, Box.Append, Box.Delete, Box.Padded, Box.SetPadded, ui.Align
  rust    -
  python  tkinter.Pack, tkinter.Place, tkinter.Frame, ttk.Frame
  note    the layout is computed by Rebel the same on every system, in wxWidgets' sizers' manner; a widget's place given by hand, `tkinter.Place`'s, is refused: it is what a layout is for

capability ui/grid  widgets in cells of columns and rows, the room left shared by the columns' and rows' weights
  heroes  ui.grid, ui.set_grid_stretch
  go      ui.NewGrid, Grid.Append, Grid.InsertAt, Grid.Padded, Grid.SetPadded, ui.At
  rust    -
  python  tkinter.Grid
  note    a cell spanning several columns is not offered; a box inside a cell holds what would span

capability ui/form  labelled fields, a label and its field on each line
  heroes  ui.grid
  go      ui.NewForm, Form.Append, Form.Delete, Form.Padded, Form.SetPadded
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    a form is a grid of two columns, labels in the first

