  rust    -
  python  tkinter.Misc.after
  note    a headless app's clock moves only as far as `wait` lets time pass, so its timers fire on the same waits on every machine

capability ui/state  a widget greyed out or used, shown or hidden, destroyed, and asked what it is
  heroes  ui.set_enabled, ui.set_visible, ui.destroy, ui.kind_of, ui.Kind
  go      ControlBase.Enable, ControlBase.Disable, ControlBase.Enabled, ControlBase.Show, ControlBase.Hide, ControlBase.Visible, ControlBase.Destroy, Window.Destroy, Box.Destroy, Form.Destroy, Group.Destroy, Tab.Destroy, Area.Destroy
  rust    -
  python  tkinter.Misc.destroy
  note    a widget whose life has ended is told `closed` by every call, never another widget's state

